                <pb facs="0410" n="338" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg338"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Minister
                        Moses.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-09-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Taking note of the steps which you
                    have taken with me toward the suppression of the abuse of the American flag by
                    its display over the saloons and wineshops at the Piraeus, I hasten to bring to
                    your knowledge that the director of police of the neighboring city has received
                    orders to exercise strict watch and prevent the abuse in question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">K. B.
                    Mavromichalis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
